atrix  whose columns are the coordinates of the vectors $T({b}_{1})$ and $T({b}_{2})$ relative to the basis $B.$ Therefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n[\\,T\\,]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-38884/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6641b2cf-00bc-5542-a566-5b8689f2f2a4"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-38884"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-38918/selection/d90a5b958a27b3f0c3a5ffb353a0daf3d409d956bcc7c6db014696caca3e461e" :answer/id #uuid "0d61ca26-0a90-54af-9db0-7dd60cd4a9ee" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & \\frac{1}{6} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{6} & \\frac{5}{6}\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-38918/selection/ddfe5c9bd62af489c9b22185a7b8a22c734c4dbd49d5bf9e78046018953cdf4d" :answer/id #uuid "bf7ca8b1-7d89-514b-a1c7-2184b24900f4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{7}{6} & \\frac{1}{6} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{6} & \\frac{5}{6}\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-38918/selection/29d68ee905e91382714bbd17a1ad6bdaa807290ff3e21c3ca6c68bf7287b76a2" :answer/id #uuid "1649d14f-54d9-5949-a983-9ee90b1747db" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -\\frac{1}{6} & \\frac{5}{6}\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-38918/selection/714155feb290f1d11803975b371823d4b6575c78ad3f4e1c23918e0f0e5ce7ca" :answer/id #uuid "c04fc26a-43fb-5262-bcfa-6cb2b3a6bb02" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{8}{6} & 2 \\\\ -\\frac{5}{6} & \\frac{5}{6}\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-38918/selection/974acc66fc897766913a66262c01da403e805d0e28b9740b5af56c75bb17e0c3" :answer/id #uuid "f1bd5202-7edb-59e5-8a10-76cb9fb6bcab" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{7}{6} & \\frac{1}{6} \\\\ \\frac{1}{6} & \\frac{5}{6}\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-38918/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "90fbf554-932a-5d03-80b4-8ca780d58d86" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-38918/selection/ddfe5c9bd62af489c9b22185a7b8a22c734c4dbd49d5bf9e78046018953cdf4d" :answer-field/choices ["q-38918/selection/d90a5b958a27b3f0c3a5ffb353a0daf3d409d956bcc7c6db014696caca3e461e" "q-38918/selection/ddfe5c9bd62af489c9b22185a7b8a22c734c4dbd49d5bf9e78046018953cdf4d" "q-38918/selection/29d68ee905e91382714bbd17a1ad6bdaa807290ff3e21c3ca6c68bf7287b76a2" "q-38918/selection/714155feb290f1d11803975b371823d4b6575c78ad3f4e1c23918e0f0e5ce7ca" "q-38918/selection/974acc66fc897766913a66262c01da403e805d0e28b9740b5af56c75bb17e0c3"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-38918" :question/id #uuid "2244cd7a-51c5-5d7a-adfd-69f19a073f69" :question/math-academy-id "q-38918" :question/problem "Let $B$ be a basis of ${R}^{2}$ and let $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ be a linear transformation. Find $[\\,T\\,]_{B}$, given that\n\n$\\,$ $T([\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}])=[\\begin{aligned}x+y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]\\,$ and $\\,B={[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]}.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's denote the vectors of $B$ as ${{b}_{1},{b}_{2}}.$ The $B$-matrix for $T$ is a matrix whose columns are the coordinates of the vectors $T({b}_{1})$ and $T({b}_{2})$ relative to the basis $B.$\n\nFirst, let's find the image of ${b}_{1}$ and ${b}_{2}$ under $T,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T({b}_{1}) & =T([\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}])=[\\begin{aligned}10 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\ T({b}_{2}) & =T([\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}])=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the coordinates of $T({b}_{1})$ and $T({b}_{2})$ relative to the basis $B$, we consider the matrix\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}| & | & | & | \\\\ {b}_{1} & {b}_{2} & T({b}_{1}) & T({b}_{2}) \\\\ | & | & | & |\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, we reduce the left-hand side to reduced row echelon form using Gaussian elimination. Then, on the right-hand side, we will obtain the $B$-matrix for $T:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}8 & -4 & 10 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 2 & 2 & 2\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{1}:=\\frac{1}{8}{R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -\\frac{1}{2} & \\frac{5}{4} & -\\frac{1}{4} \\\\ 2 & 2 & 2 & 2\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}-2{R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -\\frac{1}{2} & \\frac{5}{4} & -\\frac{1}{4} \\\\ 0 & 3 & -\\frac{1}{2} & \\frac{5}{2}\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:=\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -\\frac{1}{2} & \\frac{5}{4} & -\\frac{1}{4} \\\\ 0 & 1 & -\\frac{1}{6} & \\frac{5}{6}\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & \\frac{7}{6} & \\frac{1}{6} \\\\ 0 & 1 & -\\frac{1}{6} & \\frac{5}{6}\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n[\\,T\\,]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{7}{6} & \\frac{1}{6} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{6} & \\frac{5}{6}\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-38918/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "56260e5b-1f89-58db-8833-b8efa77b5e9f"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-38918"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-82474/selection/694bad13c5103eadba5f48c6c278f7aa54592e74dd4ba4b5e6537b89d3aec0a4" :answer/id #uuid "45cf231b-bcb0-550b-a16b-e1a5eac1516b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}7 & 8 \\\\ -4 & -3\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-82474/selection/e094069a58de1f1de8105a669ececf5bcf806984e56d3b7265a876b074897ffb" :answer/id #uuid "59707974-1c8a-5bcd-9699-b38eb1633877" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}8 & 